id: pm-web-zmbx
title: Inspect backend operations and review inputs without executing changes
description: "Backend contract explorer extending inspection from maintenance providers to all advertised project operations. Overlap rechecked: core getContracts owns command availability, schemas and runtime fields; pm-ops backend-capabilities verifies list/get/schema assurance; existing maintenance UI covers three actions. Reuse core metadata rather than implementing dispatch or assurance."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-23T14:34:25.958Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-23T15:08:33.479Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Synthetic directory, Postgres and remote adapters render consistent capabilities; unavailable providers never enable a destructive control. Typed SDK and native CLI expose bounded TOON/JSON discovery and typed refusals with remedies. Review-only forms never dispatch operations. Validate a public fleet tracker copy without git and report measured evidence; npm and Bun CI release gates pass at unchanged thresholds."
comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-23T14:36:16.105Z",codex-agent,"Overlap check: core getContracts exposes live action_availability, runtime schema and SDK input schemas; pm-ops backend-capabilities audits list/get/schema only; pm-web maintenance-provider UI gates three operations. Explorer reuses core contract reads and mutation classification. Plan: paginated SDK/native CLI and authenticated project UI, fresh fail-closed availability checks, review-only envelopes with no operation dispatch, no-git regressions, synthetic adapter parity, public tracker-copy measurements, CI npm/Bun release gates. Installed host CLI is 2026.10.23; all tracker writes use the unchanged repo pin 2026.10.20. Local npm required isolated user configuration because host allow-scripts broke Git dependency preparation."
  "2026-10-23T14:50:50.408Z",codex-agent,"Targeted linked test run passed 6/6 (zero skips). Behavioral revert proof: removing only the availability refusal in reviewContract makes the synthetic provider regression fail with Missing expected rejection; restored implementation passes. Public origin/main tracker copy: 177 certified items, 84 operations, five 20-row pages, first-page JSON 4357 bytes, 21158 ms on the loaded host; durable source hash unchanged and deletion preview executed=false. Validation ran with Git absent from PATH and a discovery ceiling above the scratch project. Database server binaries are absent locally; real SQL/HTTP route acceptance and desktop/mobile evidence run in CI. No hosted service or data was accessed."
  "2026-10-23T14:55:45.452Z",codex-agent,"PR 247 is open for review. Initial CI stopped at the unchanged zero-duplication gate: browser fixture initialization duplicated an existing test. Consolidated explorer SDK, HTTP and browser tracker setup into one shared helper; no threshold changes. Local database acceptance remains delegated to CI. Automated independent reviews are currently unavailable or skipped; no reviewer approval is claimed."
  "2026-10-23T15:08:33.473Z",codex-agent,"Full npm CI suite on Node 22 ran 821 tests: 820 passed, one existing command-inventory assertion expected 11 handlers instead of the new 12. All new SDK and real SQL/HTTP tests passed; measured coverage was 93.30% statements/lines, 83.97% branches and 96.27% functions, above unchanged thresholds. Updated the existing inventory regression to require the web contracts command and all four flags. Full gates will rerun on the corrected head."
